 "governed_sequence": [
  "1. Write recovery card into D:/QM/strategy_farm/artifacts/cards_review/<new label>.md (frontmatter ea_id/slug/source_id/g0_status APPROVED/target_symbols), bound to the original approved card of record.",
  "2. governed_magic_allocator.py --card <recovery card> (dry-run first): reserves ea_id_registry row, creates framework/EAs/<new label>/, copies card to docs/strategy_card.md, writes magic rows (ea_id*10000+slot), regenerates QM_MagicResolver.mqh, verifies. Order: dirs -> CSV -> regen -> verify -> compile.",
  "3. Copy the patched .mq5 to the new label, rewriting only #property description and the qm_ea_id input default; copy SPEC.md with the new identity header; for baskets copy basket_manifest.json and add execution_symbols/signal_only_symbols so the Q02 intake role contract is satisfied.",
  "4. Pre-seed sets/ via framework/scripts/gen_setfile.ps1 (canonical generator, build_hash stays 'pending' so no bound-setfile binding exists) so infer_timeframe resolves from existing_setfiles; baskets additionally carry the hand-authored logical host setfile copied from the predecessor with only identity comments rewritten.",
  "5. farmctl.py enqueue-compile <new label> -> governed COMPILE_EA row under the NEW id.",
  "6. After COMPILE_OK: farmctl.py intake-first-q02 (read-only plan first, then --apply) -> exactly one Q02 canary per new identity.",
  "7. tools/strategy_farm/set_priority_track.py (plan first, then --apply) binding the new Q02 rows to decisions/2026-09-13_owner_symbol_fix_priority_track.md via framework/registry/owner_priority_tracks.json."
 ],
 "identity_rule": "23.08 identity rule: a rebuilt EX5 is a new identity from Q02. The old ea_id cannot reopen Q02 (q02_append_only_rerun_requires_same_exact_source_and_rerun_row / existing_q02_row), so each patched source re-enters the chain under a new 414xx identity.",
 "no_touch": [
  "C:/QM/mt5/T_Live and every live binary",
  "every existing work_item, verdict and evidence row of the old ea_ids",
  "the old EA directories except as read-only sources"
 ],
